       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Single doses are generally capped at about 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** The ordered daily dose is about twice the maximum. That raises the risk of severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, divided, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg per dose at a different frequency\n\nTell me the intended dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is really what you want, tell me the clinical reason. I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy before it's entered."
